      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Guide\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Lore\n**Related Zones:**\n- Argin-Hiz [zone=1004]\n- Dead Hills [zone=942]\n- Ethernere Tainted West Karana [zone=939]\n- North Qeynos [zone=4]\n- North Ro 2.0 [zone=24]\n- Qeynos Hills [zone=17]\n- South Qeynos [zone=5]\n- South Ro 2.0 [zone=43]\n- Tower of Rot [zone=999]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Ambassador of Solusek Ro [npc=47257]\n- Erron Ailspoc [npc=47029]\n- Guard Jepper [npc=47258]\n- Guard Mulk [npc=47268]\n- Guard Sloop [npc=47259]\n- Lanys T`Vyl [npc=47262]\n- a Doomscale scout [npc=47251]\n- a frightened inhabitant [npc=47254]\n- an ash wind [npc=47261]\n- an ash wind [npc=47255]\n- northqeynos - Captain Deidre Harath [npc=46981]\n- northqeynos - Gahlith Wrannstad [npc=46980]\n**Related Quests:**\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Dousing the Flames [quest=7601]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Embers of the Giants [quest=7607]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Fire Prevention [quest=7602]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): No Sympathy for the Forlorn [quest=7600]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Sifting Through the Ashes [quest=7603]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Source of the Ash Wind [quest=7604]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Still the Ash Hurricane [quest=7608]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Sympathy for the Forlorn [quest=7599]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Argin-Hiz): Topple the Ash Giants [quest=7606]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Tower of Rot): Beyond the Barrier [quest=7529]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Tower of Rot): Ether Too Near [quest=7525]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Tower of Rot): From Whence They Came [quest=7526]\n- COTF Pre-Launch (Tower of Rot): Heads for the Hills [quest=7527]\n- Defender of Qeynos [quest=7528]\n- Flamewarder [quest=7605]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed May 14 05:54:27 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is an overview of pre-launch events leading up to the releases of the Tower of Rot (release: May 21, 2014) and Argin-Hiz (release: July 16, 2014)._\n\n---\n\n**Currently Live**\nJuly 4, 2014 to September 6, 2014\nSolo Task: Source of the Ash Wind [quest=7604] (Lanys T`Vyl in Ethernere Tainted West Karana - across from Lady Lendiniara)\nSolo Task: Sympathy for the Forlorn [quest=7599] (Ambassador of Solusek Ro -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nSolo Task: No Sympathy for the Forlorn [quest=7600] (a frightened inhabitant -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nSolo Task: Dousing the Flames [quest=7601] (Guard Sloop -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nSolo Task: Fire Prevention [quest=7602] (Guard Jepper -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nSolo Task: Sifting Through the Ashes [quest=7603] (a Doomscale scout -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nJuly 7, 2014 to September 6, 2014\nSolo Task: Embers of the Giants [quest=7607] (a Doomscale scout -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nSolo Task: Still the Ash Hurricane [quest=7608] (Guard Jepper -- South Ro - east of the wizard spires - map)\nSolo Task: Topple the Ash Giants [quest=7606] (Guard Mulk -- North Ro - due south of the Freeport gate - map)\n\n---\n\n**Finished Events**\nMay 14, 2014 to July 7, 2014\nSolo Task: Ether Too Near [quest=7525] (Captain Deidre in North Qeynos - next to the POK portal stone).\nSolo Task: Heads for the Hills [quest=7527] (Captain Deidre).\nShared Task: From Whence They Came [quest=7526] (Gahlith Wrannstad in North Qeynos - next to the POK portal stone).\nMay 17, 2014 to July 7, 2014\nShared Task: Beyond the Barrier [quest=7529] (Erron Ailspoc in the Dead Hills - map)\n\n---\n\n**Tower of Rot Pre-Launch Achievement**\nCompletion of all four pre-launch tasks gives you credit for the \" Defender of Qeynos [quest=7528]\" achievement (access to title - suffix: \"Defender of Qeynos\")\n\n---\n\n**Argin-Hiz Pre-Launch Achievement**\nCompletion of all nine pre-launch tasks gives you credit for the \" Flamewarder [quest=7604]\" achievement (access to title - suffix: \" , Flame Warder\")\n\n---\n\n**What's Going On: Tower of Rot**\nThe lead-up to the Tower of Rot's opening began with Captain Russell Cooper [npc=44047]'s heroic adventure chain.\nAfter having cleared a path [quest=7274] to the excavation site [quest=7275] in the Dead Hills [zone=942], you got a look at the Descending Tower [quest=7276]...\nIn time, you would encounter a rather angry Undead Lord by the name of Kyle Bayle [npc=45701], the apparent long-dead leader of the original ill-fated Qeynos expedition into the Dead Hills many years prior. While you managed to defeat Kyle Bayle's Captain and Sergeants, the Undead Lord managed to retreat back into his tower [quest=7413].\nMeanwhile, the guards of Qeynos have been trying to remedy the disaster site that is West Karana. This situation has gone unresolved, however, and creatures of the Ethernere (having initially appeared due to the time ripples caused by Lady Lendiniara [npc=44340]'s appearance) have managed to breach the Qeynos Hills [zone=17] and the city of Qeynos [zone=4], itself.\nCaptain Deidre Harath [npc=46981] has arrived to deal with the problem in Qeynos, and Gahlith Wrannstad [npc=46980] \\- one of the Qeynos caster guildmasters - has been tasked with finding a way to rid Qeynos of the Ethernere creatures for good.\nThe citizens of Qeynos aren't the only ones having a problem with the Ethernere invasion. These creatures have also begun to invade the site of the Tower of Rot, itself, and are being fought off by the tower's undead forces ( Erron Ailspoc [npc=47029] has been sent to recover some samples from these beings).\nWhat links the Tower of Rot with those time ripples is not yet known for sure, but rumors suggest something inside the tower will lead to an answer.\n\n---\n\n**What's Going On: Argin-Hiz**\n_From a June 2014 patch message:_\nWarm winds begin to blow in Ethernere-Tainted West Karana [zone=939] and the South Desert of Ro [zone=43]. Winds like these must portend the arrival of something or someone. Stay alert for when the time comes!\n_From a news announcement on July 2, 2014:_\n\"The ash pours into our lands, threatening what meager homes and crops we have! Won't you [destroy] these wandering ash monsters?\"\nA hot ash wind is blowing from the portals that have appeared in Ethernere-Tainted West Karana and South Ro. Creatures of ash have ventured out of the portals and are roaming menacingly throughout South Ro and North Ro. Guards from Freeport have come here to bring order to this region and are beseeching powerful adventurers to travel here to assist with quelling the blaze.\nFreeport guards aren't the only group thatâ€™s investigating this disturbance. Solusek Ro has sensed a form of his own power flowing from these portals, and has sent an ambassador here on his behalf to learn more.\nThe Argin-Hiz launch event has been designed for groups of level 100 characters. The first phase of the Argin-Hiz launch event begins on Friday, July 4th, 2014. The second phase will begin on Monday, July 7th, 2014. This event content will be available in game until Saturday, September 6th, 2014.\n\"You still do not trust me. I understand. Be wary of all things, but do not be foolish! We both can see that [doom] approaches.\" - Lanys T`vyl\nLanys T`vyl is waiting for you in the Ethernere-Tainted West Karana. She would like for you to further investigate this situation. The last artifact needed to send Lady Lendiniara back to her home may be located beyond the ash portals that have appeared in these areas, and the only way to know for sure is to gather other powerful allies to your side to investigate for yourself.",
