      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis is a Karana: Tempest Festival event task that runs in late April to Early May.\nYou can obtain this quest from speaking with Rosalind Mischeva in Plane of Knowledge on the west side of the zone near the pond. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Rosalind Mischeva'\nRosalind Mischeva says, 'Hail and well met. I do so enjoy a late [spring rain]. Make sure you take a moment and bask in the rain. I do so miss the [sounds of rain] during the summertime.'\nYou say, 'Late spring rain? I have noticed that it has been raining more than normal.'\nRosalind Mischeva says, '[The Tempest] blessed us with the Throne of Thunder and now he blesses us with soft rain. You should rejoice and sing his praises.'\nYou say, 'The Tempest is Karana correct?'\nRosalind Mischeva says, 'Yes, his voice is gentle on [the wind] and brings the end of spring. It is the time for the crops to grow and for the storms to ebb.'\nYou say, 'What does the wind say?'\nRosalind Mischeva says, 'I dare not speak for the Rainkeeper, but I hear that it has been raining in most of the cities. Perhaps you [could gather] the rain and return it to the sacred pond?'\nYou say, 'I could gather the rain and take it. Just let me know where to go.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Here Comes the Rain'.\nRosalind Mischeva says, 'I have marked down all the cities to visit and gather the rain. Here is a vessel to gather the rain. Make sure you center yourself before trying to collect the rain. Once the carafe has been filled take it to the sacred pool.'\nYou are given: Empty Tempest Carafe\nAll you need to do is zone into the below zones, target yourself and right click Empty Tempest Carafe.\nAn easy way of doing this is to just bind yourself in Plane of Knowledge and use the stones to get to each city.\nThey can be done in any order.\nHint: Save South Qeynos, Surefall Glade, and Jaggedpine for last. That way you can go to them one after the other and then just zone back into Surefall glade for the last step.\n- 1. Gather the rain in Plane of Knowledge 0/1 The Plane of Knowledge\n- 2. Gather the rain in South Qeynos 0/1 South Qeynos\n- 3. Gather the rain in Surefall Glade 0/1 Surefall Glade\n- 4. Gather the rain in Rivervale 0/1 Rivervale\n- 5. Gather the rain in Halas 0/1 Halas\n- 6. Gather the rain in Neriak 0/1 Neriak - Foreign Quarter\n- 7. Gather the rain in Oggok 0/1 Oggok\n- 8. Gather the rain in Grobb 0/1 Grobb\n- 9. Gather the rain in Greater Faydark 0/1 Greater Faydark\n- 10. Gather the rain in Ak'Anon 0/1 Ak'Anon\n- 11. Gather the rain in South Kaladim 0/1 South Kaladim\n- 12. Gather the rain in Southern Felwithe 0/1 Southern Felwithe\n- 13. Gather the rain in Paineel 0/1 Paineel\n- 14. Gather the rain in Cabilis East 0/1 Cabilis East\n- 15. Gather the rain in Shar Vahl 0/1 Shar Vahl\n- 16. Gather the rain in Jaggedpine Forest 0/1 Jaggedpine Forest\n- 17. Gather the rain in East Freeport 0/1 East Freeport\n- 18. Gather the rain in Crescent Reach 0/1 Crescent Reach\nAt this point your Empty Tempest Carafe disappears and on your cursor you are given a Filled Tempest Carafe.\n- 19. Pour the rain into the Surefall Glade pool 0/1 Surefall Glade\nInside of the caves, there is water fall that drops into a pool of water on the south side of this waterfall /waypoint 497, -319, -1, right click the Filled Tempest Carafe here.\nYour task 'Here Comes the Rain' has been updated.\nYou have received a replay timer for 'Here Comes the Rain': 0d:18h:0m remaining.\nYou have finished your pilgrimage of the Storm Lord and brought his blessed rain to the sacred pool.\nReward(s):\nExperience for your level\nMoney\nThis unlocks the next task, Tempest Festival - Singing in the Reign [quest=10909].Submitted by: GidonoRewards:\n[",
